From: Nicolo Giuliani <nicologiuliani6@studio.unibo.it>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: endpoint: pci-epf-vntb: poll the host commands and doorbells every 1 ms

The host has no way to interrupt the endpoint here, so doorbells are found by
polling. With HZ=100 the 5 ms period rounds up to a whole tick (10 ms) and
caps a bulk transfer at a few Mbit/s.

---
--- a/drivers/pci/endpoint/functions/pci-epf-vntb.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/endpoint/functions/pci-epf-vntb.c
@@ -319,7 +319,7 @@
 
 reset_handler:
 	queue_delayed_work(kpcintb_workqueue, &ntb->cmd_handler,
-			   msecs_to_jiffies(5));
+			   msecs_to_jiffies(1));
 }
 
 /**
